// error
// #4631, the literal half: SPEC §10.5 forbids an unexported field appearing
// in a FOREIGN composite literal, not only being read through one — "an
// unexported field is module-private (and may not appear in a foreign
// [literal])". `check_foreign_field_unexported.bit` pins the READ, which
// `vMember` judges; this pins the literal slot, which `vCompositeSlot`
// (validatezero.bit) judges through the same `vForeignFieldAccess`. Two
// entry points, one rule — without a case each, either call site could be
// dropped in a refactor and the suite would stay green.
//
// `std/uuid`'s `UUID` is the class the ticket names: `docs/stdlib/uuid.md`
// says its fields are private and that a value comes from a generator,
// `parse`, or a well-known constructor. `lo` is left out deliberately — one
// named slot is enough, and the omission is legal (it has a zero value), so
// this asserts the slot rule alone and not the E0085 omission rule.
import { UUID } from "std/uuid"

fn main() {
  let u = UUID{ hi: 1 }
  println("${u.version()}")
}
